{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>On the stones</b> Twice in the Masorah: וראיתן על האבנים / וארד בית היוצר והנה הוא עושה מלאכה על האבנים / As stated R. in ch. 1 of Sotah, the greater one conveyed to them: at the hour a woman crouches to give birth, her thighs cool like stones. Another interpretation: just as the potter — thigh on this side and thigh on that side, with the stand in the middle — so too a woman: thigh on this side and thigh on that side, with the child in the middle. Another interpretation: what has this to do with a potter? Because it is written: כי הנה כחמר ביד היוצר."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The Hebrew lists 'Twice in the Masorah' but then cites three occurrences including the lemma verse itself; the third citation (from Jeremiah 18:3) is introduced by כדאי׳ as a Talmudic prooftext rather than a Masorah occurrence, so 'Twice' likely counts only the two Exodus/Jeremiah parallels cited first."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:40.864251048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}